ability and expression of MLH-1 and hMSH2 in sebaceous gland carcinomas as markers for Muir-Torre Syndrome</article-title><source>Clin Cancer Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>1784</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10815898</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Farrell</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Plotkin</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic causes of brain tumors: Neurofibromatosis, tuberous sclerosis, von Hippel-Lidau, and other syndromes</article-title><source>Neurol Clin</source><year>2007</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>925</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17964021</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Honchel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Halling</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaid</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pittelkow</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thibodeau</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Microsatellite instability in Muir-Torre syndrome</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1994</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>1159</fpage><lpage>63</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8118799</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kruse</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Lamberti</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruelfs</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruns</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Esche</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Is the mismatch repair deficient type of Muir-Torre syndrome confined to mutations in the hMSH2 gene?</article-title><source>Hum Genet</source><year>1996</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>747</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8931714</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kruse</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>R&#x000fc;tten</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lamberti</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosseiny-Malayeri</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruelfs</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Muir-Torre phenotype has a frequency of DNA mismatch-repair-gene mutations similar to that in hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal cancer families defined by the Amsterdam criteria</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>1998</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9634524</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kruse</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruzicka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA mismatch repair and the significance of a sebaceous skin tumor for visceral cancer prevention</article-title><source>Trends Mol Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>136</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15102357</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-